WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Let's follow the path of Dusty's trail, oh Dusty's trail, Dusty's trail.

00:08.000 --> 00:16.000
A stage and a wagon are heading west, part of a wagon train lost from the rest.

00:16.000 --> 00:24.000
Dusty's the reason for their plight, thanks to Dusty nothing's right.

00:24.000 --> 00:32.000
Only the wagon master's hand keeps them a-rollin' through the promised land.

00:32.000 --> 00:38.000
All the goin' gets mighty rough, but they don't seem to mind.

00:38.000 --> 00:44.000
It's California, eh, that's the place they must find.

00:44.000 --> 00:51.000
Deserts and rocks are in their way, but they won't stop, come what may.

00:51.000 --> 00:56.000
Mountains and hills that they must scale, but they know they'll make it,

00:56.000 --> 01:22.000
cause they just can't fail on Dusty's trail.

01:26.000 --> 01:48.000
Nice bear, good bear, go away bear, go away.

01:48.000 --> 01:52.000
Oh no, the trees on the bear's side. Help, somebody help.

01:52.000 --> 02:02.000
Go away bear, go away bear.

02:02.000 --> 02:18.000
Go away bear, go away. Help, somebody help.

02:18.000 --> 02:33.000
Help, somebody help.

02:33.000 --> 02:53.000
Help, somebody help.

02:53.000 --> 03:15.000
Help, somebody help.

03:15.000 --> 03:19.000
Something wrong with your paw, fella?

03:19.000 --> 03:26.000
Here, let me see.

03:26.000 --> 03:30.000
Look, I won't hurt you, I just want to take a look at it.

03:30.000 --> 03:33.000
Take a look. Oh, you got a fawn in your paw.

03:33.000 --> 03:36.000
Here, let me have it and I'll see if I can get it out.

03:36.000 --> 03:39.000
It might be a little painful.

03:39.000 --> 03:42.000
You wanna bite on a bullet, huh?

03:42.000 --> 03:45.000
I know, I'll just tell you a little story and you won't think about it.

03:45.000 --> 03:59.000
See, it was this little girl with golden hair and she played around with brothers like you.

03:59.000 --> 04:11.000
You're welcome.

04:11.000 --> 04:16.000
Andy, when on earth do we get our breakfast? The room service here is simply atrocious.

04:16.000 --> 04:20.000
I'm sorry Mr. Brookhaven, but I can't cook breakfast until Dusty gets back with the firewood.

04:20.000 --> 04:23.000
He should have been back by now.

04:23.000 --> 04:27.000
Oh, there he is now. Is that a bear following him?

04:27.000 --> 04:30.000
Sure is.

04:30.000 --> 04:34.000
Dusty, duck. It's not a duck, it's a bear.

04:34.000 --> 04:37.000
Run before he attacks you. Everybody head for cover.

04:37.000 --> 04:41.000
Dusty, look out.

04:41.000 --> 04:45.000
Carter, why do you always hide behind me when there's danger?

04:45.000 --> 04:48.000
Because it's safer, my dear.

04:48.000 --> 04:50.000
Yes, of course.

04:50.000 --> 04:55.000
Dusty, get out of my line of fire.

04:55.000 --> 04:57.000
Don't shoot him, he's a friend of mine.

04:57.000 --> 05:03.000
Dusty, there's no such thing as a friendly bear.

05:03.000 --> 05:08.000
You're going to flee. Isn't that right, Hercules?

05:08.000 --> 05:12.000
Dusty, what's the matter with you? Will you get away from the bear before he tears you apart?

05:12.000 --> 05:14.000
He wouldn't do that after what I did for him.

05:14.000 --> 05:15.000
What do you mean?

05:15.000 --> 05:23.000
He had a thorn in his paw and I pulled it out and he likes me so much now he won't let me out of his sight.

05:23.000 --> 05:28.000
I don't believe it.

05:28.000 --> 05:31.000
It's just like Andrew Cleese and the lion.

05:31.000 --> 05:34.000
Andrew, what's his name when a lion got to do that?

05:34.000 --> 05:40.000
Well, you see, Andrew Cleese was a Roman slave and he was supposed to fight a lion in the arena.

05:40.000 --> 05:45.000
But the lion spared the boy's life because many years before the boy had removed a thorn from the lion's foot.

05:45.000 --> 05:53.000
But the bear is man's natural enemy. He's liable to attack any one of us at any time.

05:53.000 --> 05:57.000
No, no. I mean, look at that cute white stripe on his nose there. I'm going to keep him.

05:57.000 --> 06:04.000
You are not going to keep that man killer here. I insist you get rid of him.

06:04.000 --> 06:07.000
You see, you see, he misses.

06:07.000 --> 06:10.000
No, he isn't. It's not the way you yelled at me.

06:10.000 --> 06:11.000
What?

06:11.000 --> 06:16.000
Dusty's right. He thought you were going to harm Dusty so he protected him just like he would one of his own cubs.

06:16.000 --> 06:22.000
But Dusty is not one of his own cubs.

06:22.000 --> 06:26.000
Easy, big boy, easy. Mr. Brookhaven didn't mean it, did you, Mr. Brookhaven?

06:26.000 --> 06:34.000
No, no, no, no. No, I didn't mean it at all.

06:34.000 --> 06:40.000
Dusty, Mr. Callahan won't like you having a bear around camp.

06:40.000 --> 06:45.000
Mr. Callahan, we'll be back from Scouting Owasso Pass for two more days and by that time you'll be in love with Hercules, you'll see.

06:45.000 --> 06:47.000
But we're afraid to leave the wagon with him around.

06:47.000 --> 06:49.000
You don't have to be afraid. He won't harm you.

06:49.000 --> 06:52.000
That's what they tried to tell Little Red Riding Hood.

06:52.000 --> 06:56.000
Oh, he's very tame. I even taught him to shake hands. Show, show the girls.

06:56.000 --> 06:58.000
Ah!

06:58.000 --> 07:00.000
He's keeping away from us.

07:00.000 --> 07:02.000
Well, I thought they'd teach him some manners.

07:02.000 --> 07:04.000
Ah!

07:08.000 --> 07:10.000
Dusty!

07:10.000 --> 07:15.000
We absolutely protest having this blasted bear join this party.

07:15.000 --> 07:17.000
This is a wagon train, not Noah's Ark.

07:17.000 --> 07:23.000
Don't worry, Mr. Brookhaven. When we hit the trail again, Mr. Callahan gets back. I'm sure we'll leave the grizzly behind.

07:23.000 --> 07:28.000
Oh, I certainly hope so. I mean, he really does have atrocious breath.

07:28.000 --> 07:29.000
Where is the bear?

07:29.000 --> 07:31.000
Well, he's out in the woods someplace.

07:31.000 --> 07:34.000
Come along, dear. It's our siesta time anyway.

07:38.000 --> 07:40.000
Look out, a little look.

07:40.000 --> 07:45.000
Good heavens. Same thing happened to Goldilocks.

07:52.000 --> 07:59.000
Dusty, as the owner of this wagon train, I absolutely insist that you get rid of that lumbering quadruped.

07:59.000 --> 08:03.000
I don't think he liked what you called him. He doesn't mean to frighten you. He's just not on wagon train broke yet.

08:03.000 --> 08:10.000
Wagon train broke? He is a menace.

08:11.000 --> 08:22.000
Now look here. You K-E-E-P that B-E-A-R out of our way or you'll be without a J-O-B.

08:23.000 --> 08:26.000
Careful, I think he can spell.

08:26.000 --> 08:33.000
I'm so S-O-R-R-Y.

08:40.000 --> 08:41.000
Where's Dusty?

08:41.000 --> 08:44.000
Oh, he took Hercules fishing for tonight's supper.

08:44.000 --> 08:48.000
That awful bear pulled our wash off the line and tore it into ribbons. Look at this.

08:48.000 --> 08:52.000
Look what he did to my... It's useless.

08:52.000 --> 08:57.000
Mr. Callahan will hear Dusty would have gotten rid of that bear a long time ago.

08:57.000 --> 08:59.000
Now look what he's doing.

09:01.000 --> 09:06.000
Son of a gun. Get out of the food, Hercules.

09:15.000 --> 09:17.000
Andy, are you all right?

09:17.000 --> 09:19.000
Oh, yeah, I think so.

09:19.000 --> 09:22.000
Hi. Did Hercules come back here?

09:22.000 --> 09:24.000
He came back.

09:24.000 --> 09:26.000
Come on, Betsy.

09:26.000 --> 09:30.000
I sent him home because he was naughty. Look, he ate all the fish I caught.

09:31.000 --> 09:36.000
Dusty, I think it would be better for everybody if you got rid of that bear.

09:36.000 --> 09:38.000
Just because he ate some fish?

09:38.000 --> 09:41.000
No, because he stole our food supply and because he belted me.

09:41.000 --> 09:43.000
That couldn't have been Hercules. That had to be another bear.

09:43.000 --> 09:45.000
It was Hercules. It wasn't another bear.

09:45.000 --> 09:50.000
Oh, what if Hercules apologizes to you? What if I put him on a leash?

09:51.000 --> 09:53.000
I know, I'll put a muzzle on him.

09:54.000 --> 09:56.000
How about if I take him to the woods and...

10:06.000 --> 10:09.000
Well, this is the place we met and this is the place we say goodbye.

10:09.000 --> 10:13.000
I hate to do it to you, old fella, but nobody around here likes you except me.

10:13.000 --> 10:17.000
Oh, look, don't look at me that way. I hate to see a grown bear cry.

10:20.000 --> 10:22.000
So long, little pal.

10:38.000 --> 10:42.000
Poor Dusty. He's been sitting back there like that all night.

10:42.000 --> 10:47.000
I didn't think he'd miss the beast. Only one bear misses another bear that much.

10:48.000 --> 10:50.000
Oh, well, he'll get used to it.

10:50.000 --> 10:52.000
I hope so.

11:04.000 --> 11:06.000
We've got company.

11:06.000 --> 11:08.000
I wonder who those men are.

11:08.000 --> 11:10.000
I wonder if they're single.

11:10.000 --> 11:13.000
Oh dear, someone's coming to call and I'm not even dressed.

11:13.000 --> 11:15.000
How dare they drop in before breakfast.

11:20.000 --> 11:21.000
Howdy.

11:21.000 --> 11:22.000
Howdy, what can we do for you?

11:22.000 --> 11:23.000
Name's Blake.

11:23.000 --> 11:24.000
Mine's Kim.

11:24.000 --> 11:26.000
Oh, it's nice to meet you. My name's Andy. This is Dusty.

11:26.000 --> 11:27.000
Howdy.

11:27.000 --> 11:28.000
Howdy.

11:28.000 --> 11:30.000
Oh, hey. See any bears around here?

11:31.000 --> 11:32.000
Bears?

11:32.000 --> 11:34.000
Well, I thought they kept to the high country.

11:34.000 --> 11:37.000
Well, lately a lot of them have been raiding the ranches in these parts,

11:37.000 --> 11:39.000
killing livestock and attacking folks.

11:39.000 --> 11:40.000
Is that a fact?

11:40.000 --> 11:42.000
We're shooting those critters on sight.

11:42.000 --> 11:44.000
Shooting them on sight?

11:44.000 --> 11:46.000
Yeah, they're killers.

11:46.000 --> 11:48.000
You folks better be on the lookout.

11:48.000 --> 11:50.000
Those bears that just as soon attack you as look at you.

11:56.000 --> 11:57.000
Just a minute, Dusty.

11:57.000 --> 11:59.000
No, I'm in a hurry. I gotta find Hercules.

11:59.000 --> 12:02.000
Now, you know, I could have made a mistake about Hercules hitting me.

12:02.000 --> 12:04.000
It could have been another bear.

12:04.000 --> 12:07.000
In fact, now that I think about it, I don't believe he had a white mark on his nose.

12:07.000 --> 12:11.000
Well, it's nice of you to admit it, Andy, but I'll apologize to Hercules for you.

12:11.000 --> 12:14.000
If you don't mind, I'd like to come with you and apologize myself.

12:14.000 --> 12:15.000
You want to help me find him?

12:15.000 --> 12:16.000
Sure.

12:16.000 --> 12:17.000
Well, thanks.

12:27.000 --> 12:28.000
See any bear tracks?

12:28.000 --> 12:30.000
Hercules gotta be around here someplace.

12:30.000 --> 12:33.000
Hercules! Yoo-hoo, Hercules!

12:33.000 --> 12:35.000
We better split up.

12:35.000 --> 12:37.000
Why don't you cover this area and I'll look over here.

12:37.000 --> 12:39.000
Okay. If you see him, give me a yell.

12:39.000 --> 12:40.000
Yeah, right.

12:51.000 --> 12:53.000
Where can that bear be?

12:56.000 --> 12:57.000
There he is.

12:57.000 --> 12:59.000
That's him, all right.

12:59.000 --> 13:02.000
He's got that white mark on his nose.

13:02.000 --> 13:05.000
I'm not going to make that mistake again.

13:07.000 --> 13:09.000
Dusty! I found him!

13:09.000 --> 13:11.000
What is it, Andy?

13:12.000 --> 13:15.000
I found Hercules. Come on.

13:15.000 --> 13:17.000
He's over here.

13:18.000 --> 13:20.000
Right down here.

13:20.000 --> 13:27.000
Hercules, we've come to take you back.

13:35.000 --> 13:37.000
What are you doing down there?

13:38.000 --> 13:40.000
I ran into the wrong grizzly again.

13:40.000 --> 13:42.000
Are you sure it wasn't Hercules?

13:42.000 --> 13:44.000
You know, I could have sworn it was,

13:44.000 --> 13:47.000
but the bear that decked me was a complete stranger.

13:47.000 --> 13:49.000
Terrific laugh.

13:49.000 --> 13:51.000
We've got to keep looking.

13:55.000 --> 13:57.000
I don't see any sign of Andy or Dusty.

13:57.000 --> 13:59.000
Why didn't they take their horses?

13:59.000 --> 14:01.000
It's going to take them forever to walk back.

14:01.000 --> 14:03.000
Bears frighten horses.

14:03.000 --> 14:04.000
Me too.

14:04.000 --> 14:08.000
And up to now I never thought I'd have anything in common with a horse.

14:09.000 --> 14:11.000
Aren't Andy and Dusty here yet?

14:11.000 --> 14:12.000
No, sir, they're not.

14:12.000 --> 14:14.000
I wish they'd hurry.

14:14.000 --> 14:16.000
By the time we get to California,

14:16.000 --> 14:19.000
there won't be enough gold left to fill my teeth.

14:19.000 --> 14:21.000
Look!

14:23.000 --> 14:24.000
Good heavens!

14:24.000 --> 14:26.000
It's one of those killer bears.

14:27.000 --> 14:29.000
If it weren't, it would have attacked us.

14:29.000 --> 14:31.000
That's Hercules.

14:31.000 --> 14:33.000
He's faster than Andy and Dusty.

14:37.000 --> 14:38.000
Is something the matter?

14:38.000 --> 14:40.000
It's another one of those bears.

14:40.000 --> 14:46.000
It can't make out whether it's friend or foe.

14:46.000 --> 14:49.000
Hercules, now you get out of there right now.

15:00.000 --> 15:01.000
Oh, no.

15:01.000 --> 15:05.000
It may look like Hercules and it may sound like Hercules,

15:05.000 --> 15:07.000
but it certainly is not.

15:07.000 --> 15:08.000
What's his name?

15:08.000 --> 15:10.000
Back to the coach, my dear.

15:10.000 --> 15:12.000
Gold to women first.

15:12.000 --> 15:14.000
For age before beauty.

15:16.000 --> 15:18.000
He's coming after us.

15:18.000 --> 15:35.000
There's no place to hide.

15:39.000 --> 15:41.000
It's Hercules.

15:41.000 --> 15:43.000
Look at him, Hercules.

15:43.000 --> 15:45.000
Get him!

15:45.000 --> 16:08.000
Get him, Hercules!

16:15.000 --> 16:16.000
Thank you, Hercules.

16:16.000 --> 16:18.000
Thank you.

16:20.000 --> 16:23.000
Oh, I'll shake hands with you any day, honey.

16:30.000 --> 16:32.000
Sorry we couldn't find Hercules.

16:32.000 --> 16:35.000
I guess he must have headed back up to High Country.

16:35.000 --> 16:37.000
Do you see what I see?

16:37.000 --> 16:38.000
Your mouth wide.

16:38.000 --> 16:40.000
That's it.

16:40.000 --> 16:41.000
That's it.

16:41.000 --> 16:42.000
That's it.

16:42.000 --> 16:45.000
Your mouth wide, Dad.

16:45.000 --> 16:47.000
Dad, what have you got?

16:51.000 --> 16:52.000
Oh, Hercules.

16:52.000 --> 16:54.000
It's so good to see you again.

16:54.000 --> 16:56.000
What's going on?

16:56.000 --> 17:00.000
We are giving a testimonial dinner for this magnificent animal.

17:00.000 --> 17:02.000
Hercules saved our lives.

17:02.000 --> 17:05.000
We were attacked by this ferocious bear and all of a sudden they...

17:05.000 --> 17:07.000
Oh, dear.

17:09.000 --> 17:10.000
It's those two ranchers.

17:10.000 --> 17:11.000
Oh, no.

17:11.000 --> 17:13.000
Now you see, Hercules, they'll sight him and shoot.

17:13.000 --> 17:15.000
Quick, let's get him into the wagon.

17:15.000 --> 17:16.000
Come on, Hercules, hurry.

17:16.000 --> 17:17.000
Come on.

17:17.000 --> 17:18.000
Come on.

17:18.000 --> 17:19.000
Come on.

17:19.000 --> 17:20.000
Your stomach.

